name: omakase-base
version: 0.30.0

# The base harness declares no gates: enforcement comes from the custom
# harness installed with `omakase init <source>`, whose own
# payload/omakase.manifest shadows this file on the merge (delta wins).
# A harness declares one `gate:` block per check, run at the named git hook:
# omakase reports the run in the scorecard (omakase status), passes the
# check's exit code through (non-zero blocks the commit/push), and — with
# cacheable: — reuses a PASS until HEAD moves. Skip one gate once with
# OMAKASE_SKIP_<NAME>=1; skip every gate once with OMAKASE_SKIP_GATES=1
# (both audited and printed).
#
# A harness may also declare `advisory:` blocks — session-start checks that
# print a line when something needs attention and never block (run:, and an
# optional purpose:, are their only keys).
#
# See docs/authoring.md in Yuncun/omakase-harness for the gate: and advisory:
# schemas and a worked example gate.
